WEBVTT

00:25.800 --> 00:36.760
By a gentle wave

00:38.940 --> 00:47.850
saraware nagara

00:38.940 --> 00:47.850
I was swept away

00:53.020 --> 01:04.160
sotto sotto

00:53.020 --> 01:04.160
Softly, softly

01:06.500 --> 01:14.100
kokoro ga kanjiteta

01:06.500 --> 01:14.100
I felt it in my heart

01:35.610 --> 01:36.700
Okay!

01:36.700 --> 01:37.700
Today I'll get it!

01:46.460 --> 01:47.120
One... two!

01:47.120 --> 01:48.210
One... two!

01:55.590 --> 01:57.130
What are you doing?

02:05.350 --> 02:08.770
I'm sure there are much better words to greet people with...

02:09.850 --> 02:10.520
I mean...

02:15.650 --> 02:16.860
You know... I put money in, but nothing came out.

02:16.860 --> 02:19.110
You know... I put money in, but nothing came out.

02:21.990 --> 02:22.740
Are you listening?

02:24.910 --> 02:28.080
That's because it's a fairly old model.

02:30.500 --> 02:31.580
Huh? Is that yours?

02:31.580 --> 02:32.630
Huh? Is that yours?

02:33.880 --> 02:34.710
Yeah.

02:35.130 --> 02:37.340
I wanted to take a picture of the sunrise...

02:37.840 --> 02:38.590
Sunrise?

02:38.840 --> 02:39.680
Yes.

02:40.130 --> 02:42.260
The moment when the night changes into blue sky...

02:42.260 --> 02:43.220
That instant.

02:50.900 --> 02:52.350
The night... changes into blue sky.

02:52.350 --> 02:53.560
The night... changes into blue sky.

02:53.860 --> 02:54.690
Yeah.

02:55.020 --> 02:56.780
You'll be able to see it in just a moment.

02:59.650 --> 03:02.200
Okay, since it's come to this...

03:07.200 --> 03:10.460
Warm

03:07.200 --> 03:09.710
Cold

03:10.290 --> 03:11.080
Here.

03:13.290 --> 03:14.170
Huh?

03:16.460 --> 03:19.220
Bean Soup

03:16.460 --> 03:19.220
Tomato

03:17.050 --> 03:18.880
Tomato bean soup?

03:22.970 --> 03:30.230
When the night falls for the people,

03:30.230 --> 03:37.230
and the voices of people disappear,

03:37.230 --> 03:44.870
the dwellers of night step into darkness.

04:01.340 --> 04:06.140
Sky-Colored Umbrella

04:08.220 --> 04:09.600
A girl?

04:09.810 --> 04:10.640
Yeah.

04:10.980 --> 04:13.730
She said something about her can of juice getting stuck...

04:13.940 --> 04:15.350
At four in the morning?

04:15.480 --> 04:17.110
At four in the morning.

04:17.690 --> 04:19.110
Strange, isn't it?

04:19.530 --> 04:23.780
Thanks to that, even though the weather was good, I didn't get my picture.

04:24.820 --> 04:26.820
Good weather, huh?

04:29.160 --> 04:32.620
You just don't get bored of taking pictures of the sky, do you?

04:32.870 --> 04:34.420
There's no way it could get boring.

04:34.670 --> 04:36.920
There are so many changes.

04:37.670 --> 04:40.170
But people change too, don't they?

04:40.300 --> 04:41.550
I can see them.

04:46.930 --> 04:47.850
Idiot.

04:52.520 --> 04:53.140
So... what do you want?

04:53.140 --> 04:54.270
So... what do you want?

04:55.560 --> 04:56.980
What do I want?

04:56.980 --> 04:58.400
I came to get you...

04:58.770 --> 05:00.480
Homeroom is over.

05:02.030 --> 05:03.780
It's already this late?

05:03.780 --> 05:06.030
As expected, you hadn't noticed.

05:06.410 --> 05:08.530
We better get the shopping done quickly.

05:08.870 --> 05:10.530
There's no need to worry about that...

05:11.370 --> 05:13.040
because I bought it yesterday.

05:16.790 --> 05:21.920
You see, I heard that girls like quirky things, like this.

05:22.760 --> 05:24.130
What do you think?

05:24.130 --> 05:24.880
Trash.

05:24.880 --> 05:25.800
Horrible.

05:25.800 --> 05:27.050
It makes no sense.

05:29.760 --> 05:32.430
They just don't understand how cute you are.

05:32.680 --> 05:35.940
Where do you get that confidence?

05:36.140 --> 05:40.360
Okay, stop doing gross things and let's hurry.

06:17.770 --> 06:19.400
Dessert Cake Menu

06:29.740 --> 06:30.660
Hold this.

06:31.070 --> 06:32.530
Close your eyes.

06:32.910 --> 06:33.700
Okay!

06:40.120 --> 06:41.000
Open them.

06:45.210 --> 06:46.590
That's amazing!

06:46.590 --> 06:48.970
How did you do that?

06:48.970 --> 06:50.010
It's a secret.

06:55.560 --> 06:56.930
Mana-san!

06:57.730 --> 06:59.390
It's onee-chan, isn't it?

06:59.770 --> 07:01.350
Sorry.

07:01.560 --> 07:05.360
That feels very out of place to me.

07:05.360 --> 07:06.730
Yes, yes.

07:07.030 --> 07:08.900
Hello, Koyori-chan.

07:09.820 --> 07:10.700
Yorito-san!

07:11.240 --> 07:12.240
Thanks for taking care of Mana-

07:13.910 --> 07:16.700
I mean, of my sister.

07:16.990 --> 07:18.160
No, no.

07:18.160 --> 07:21.170
I feel the same. Thank you for always visiting my sister.

07:21.500 --> 07:23.130
Don't be silly!

07:23.130 --> 07:26.960
Thank you for always letting me visit.

07:27.250 --> 07:29.590
Her etiquette is perfect, as always.

07:30.380 --> 07:32.260
Are you two really sisters?

07:32.630 --> 07:33.470
Shut up!

07:33.840 --> 07:34.640
Yorito.

07:37.060 --> 07:37.890
You're late.

07:38.770 --> 07:39.480
Sorry.

07:39.810 --> 07:42.390
We had a bit of a detour today.

07:42.810 --> 07:43.940
Detour?

07:51.950 --> 07:53.410
A cake!

07:54.030 --> 07:55.990
What's this for?

07:56.410 --> 07:59.080
It's a bit late, but... happy birthday.

07:59.080 --> 08:00.700
It's a bit late, but... happy birthday.

08:02.710 --> 08:04.460
Could it be... that you don't like cake?

08:04.460 --> 08:06.460
Could it be... that you don't like cake?

08:06.880 --> 08:07.880
Not at all.

08:08.420 --> 08:10.710
Well then, here's a present from me.

08:13.340 --> 08:14.430
It's cute, isn't it?!

08:14.720 --> 08:16.600
Since it was your birthday...

08:17.010 --> 08:19.680
I spent quite a while deciding what to pick...

08:21.480 --> 08:24.190
and I was confident about that one.

08:24.190 --> 08:27.610
That's why I asked, where does that confidence come from?

08:28.190 --> 08:33.490
Well then, let's lighten the mood by lighting the candles!

08:38.700 --> 08:39.490
Mana.

08:40.240 --> 08:40.830
Yes?

08:41.620 --> 08:42.870
Thank you.

08:51.170 --> 08:53.590
That's a really loud noise.

08:53.590 --> 08:55.340
I only heard it second-hand...

08:55.340 --> 08:58.430
but apparently the church's clock tower is broken.

08:58.760 --> 08:59.720
Church?

09:01.140 --> 09:02.930
The one that's supposed to be demolished-

09:02.930 --> 09:03.810
Don't open them.

09:04.230 --> 09:04.980
Sorry.

09:09.110 --> 09:10.070
I'm going to take a quick picture.

09:10.070 --> 09:11.690
Hang on, Yorito!

09:12.070 --> 09:13.150
Geez.

09:51.570 --> 09:54.440
Will you stop going into such a trance?

09:54.690 --> 09:58.450
We didn't even eat the cake, and then visiting hours were over.

09:58.780 --> 10:01.910
Well, it was too pretty. I just...

10:02.330 --> 10:04.580
It was your sister's birthday!

10:05.250 --> 10:07.210
We'll have another one later.

10:08.250 --> 10:11.590
You're the only family that can celebrate it with her anymore.

10:11.880 --> 10:13.380
And still you...

10:13.380 --> 10:14.710
I know.

10:14.710 --> 10:16.340
My bad.

10:16.340 --> 10:20.010
Anyway, whenever you look at the sunset, it's the same.

10:20.390 --> 10:22.680
It's not like the sky is going to run away.

10:23.060 --> 10:24.220
That's not true.

10:26.310 --> 10:28.230
No two skies are the same.

10:28.600 --> 10:30.150
They're all different.

10:30.560 --> 10:31.360
That's why...

10:34.860 --> 10:36.780
Don't we have any medicine for you?

10:39.400 --> 10:41.320
Let's see...

10:43.200 --> 10:44.330
Out of ginger.

10:46.950 --> 10:47.960
Man...

10:47.960 --> 10:50.330
she should at least have ginger on hand.

10:50.620 --> 10:52.830
Stupid Mana!

11:03.720 --> 11:06.640
Can't you hide in a place that's easier for me to find?

11:23.620 --> 11:25.990
It's really coming down now.

11:31.540 --> 11:32.580
One... two!

11:32.580 --> 11:33.540
One... two!

11:36.920 --> 11:37.880
Geez.

11:39.670 --> 11:40.720
One...

11:51.100 --> 11:52.100
The sky...

12:02.860 --> 12:04.530
You're...

12:10.700 --> 12:11.960
You're...

12:13.120 --> 12:14.630
Is it stuck again?

12:15.790 --> 12:16.540
Yeah.

12:17.710 --> 12:19.380
Why don't you just go to a convenience store?

12:21.010 --> 12:22.970
Because they don't sell it.

12:23.180 --> 12:24.800
Is that really tasty?

12:24.800 --> 12:26.050
It's delicious.

12:28.060 --> 12:29.640
You don't believe me, do you?

12:31.020 --> 12:32.520
Well...

12:32.520 --> 12:33.890
It really is!

12:34.230 --> 12:35.400
Hold this.

12:37.230 --> 12:38.070
What?

12:40.320 --> 12:41.360
Get out the way.

12:42.150 --> 12:43.700
O-Okay.

12:43.860 --> 12:44.610
One... two!

12:44.610 --> 12:44.950
One... two!

12:45.780 --> 12:46.370
Wai-

12:50.660 --> 12:53.410
Ow...

12:53.410 --> 12:55.460
Don't just jump out like that!

12:56.420 --> 12:59.250
Well, I thought you would hurt you leg again-

13:16.310 --> 13:17.350
Yeah, I'm fine.

13:17.350 --> 13:18.480
Yeah, I'm fine.

13:18.480 --> 13:21.020
I'll come home as soon as it slows down a bit.

13:21.440 --> 13:22.690
Yep, bye.

13:26.820 --> 13:27.610
Here.

13:28.870 --> 13:31.280
Just pretend you were tricked, okay?

13:48.760 --> 13:50.010
I've been tricked.

13:51.390 --> 13:53.640
I think you should stock up on them now.

13:53.640 --> 13:55.680
I don't think they'll be on sale for long.

13:56.140 --> 13:57.810
But it's so tasty...

14:04.030 --> 14:05.280
Rain...

14:06.950 --> 14:09.410
Do you like the rain?

14:11.200 --> 14:13.700
I'm not sure if I like it or hate it.

14:13.700 --> 14:15.620
Because you can't see the sky anymore.

14:16.040 --> 14:18.250
You like the sky?

14:18.580 --> 14:19.210
Yeah.

14:19.500 --> 14:21.290
Remember what I was doing yesterday?

14:21.290 --> 14:24.090
I like taking pictures of lots of different skies like that.

14:24.420 --> 14:26.840
Then do you have lots of pictures of the sky?

14:26.840 --> 14:28.130
Y-Yeah.

14:28.130 --> 14:28.880
Y-Yeah.

14:29.300 --> 14:30.470
Are you interested in them?

14:32.510 --> 14:33.350
Yes.

14:33.850 --> 14:35.560
Because I also have one.

14:35.970 --> 14:37.560
It's just one, but...

14:39.940 --> 14:41.610
What beautiful red clouds.

14:41.900 --> 14:43.690
Red clouds?

14:43.690 --> 14:45.280
Clouds that have been dyed red.

14:45.780 --> 14:48.030
There are lots of different skies as well.

14:48.570 --> 14:49.320
Sunrise, sunset, blue sky, good weather, rainbow and dusk.

14:54.160 --> 14:55.660
For clouds, there are fleecy clouds,
rain clouds, cirrostratus and altostratus.

14:59.540 --> 15:01.500
When it's summer, there are cumulonimbus.

15:01.500 --> 15:03.500
When it's autumn, there are cirrocumulus.

15:03.500 --> 15:04.500
They're all different.

15:04.880 --> 15:06.170
I see.

15:06.590 --> 15:09.260
Next time, watch them carefully.

15:11.890 --> 15:13.090
Sunrise, sunset, blue sky, good weather.

15:14.640 --> 15:15.430
Hey!

15:16.260 --> 15:17.220
Fleecy clouds, rain clouds, cirrostratus, altostratus.

15:20.230 --> 15:22.230
When it's summer, there are cumulonimbus.

15:22.230 --> 15:24.190
When it's autumn, there are cirrocumulus.

15:24.560 --> 15:25.570
Any others?

15:26.940 --> 15:29.570
There are lenticularis and scattered clouds.

15:30.740 --> 15:31.860
Lenticularis, scattered clouds.

15:31.860 --> 15:33.030
Lenticularis, scattered clouds.

15:33.570 --> 15:35.030
There are a lot.

16:05.060 --> 16:06.110
Thanks.

16:06.480 --> 16:08.070
You've taught me a lot.

16:10.360 --> 16:12.030
I'll give that umbrella to you.

16:12.030 --> 16:12.650
Bye.

16:13.030 --> 16:13.700
Wait!

16:17.620 --> 16:18.830
What's your... name?

16:18.830 --> 16:19.700
What's your... name?

16:21.750 --> 16:22.540
What's yours?

16:24.830 --> 16:25.790
Yorito.

16:25.790 --> 16:27.040
Morimiya Yorito.

16:28.670 --> 16:29.710
Yorito...

16:30.510 --> 16:31.300
And yours?

16:34.970 --> 16:35.760
Matsuri.

16:35.930 --> 16:37.050
Shihou Matsuri.

16:38.720 --> 16:39.810
Matsuri...

16:41.730 --> 16:42.180
Bye.

16:59.280 --> 17:00.950
Express Home Delivery

17:17.680 --> 17:19.050
I'm hungry.

17:30.940 --> 17:32.820
He's probably just spacing out...

17:32.820 --> 17:34.950
He said he had something to do.

17:35.740 --> 17:38.620
He said he'd be going straight home, without visiting the hospital today.

17:42.950 --> 17:45.290
I asked him what had happened.

17:45.540 --> 17:47.750
But he never answered me.

17:48.080 --> 17:49.380
Yorito did?

17:49.380 --> 17:50.040
Seven.

17:52.340 --> 17:52.960
Eight.

17:53.630 --> 17:54.710
Um... I'm very sorry...

17:54.710 --> 17:57.130
Um... I'm very sorry...

17:57.130 --> 18:00.220
but I'll call you on these cards.

18:01.260 --> 18:02.350
Geez.

18:02.350 --> 18:05.560
At times like this, you don't have to be so apologetic...

18:05.930 --> 18:07.140
Sorry...

18:07.560 --> 18:09.650
Yorito is with the sky again?

18:10.270 --> 18:13.900
It's probably related to the sky.

18:15.030 --> 18:15.820
I see.

18:23.410 --> 18:25.830
You made me wait this long for onigiri?

18:26.120 --> 18:27.830
It couldn't be helped... since you asked for the impossible.

18:29.920 --> 18:31.670
I just wanted... to have some foie gras.

18:34.880 --> 18:36.590
That's why I got that.

18:37.130 --> 18:39.840
Lately, that convenience store has become more sophisticated.

18:40.390 --> 18:43.810
Foie       Gras

18:40.800 --> 18:42.010
It's foie gras flavor.

18:42.510 --> 18:43.810
You're horrible.

18:46.890 --> 18:48.520
What a bothersome lady.

18:48.850 --> 18:51.060
So, did you find her?

18:53.310 --> 18:53.730
Yeah.

18:54.570 --> 18:56.320
I have a rough idea of where she is.

18:57.440 --> 18:59.490
This time we'll meet her, right?

19:05.540 --> 19:06.790
Probably.

19:39.940 --> 19:41.360
This church....

20:42.590 --> 20:45.720
I'm glad we met sooner than I had expected.

20:48.640 --> 20:50.890
No       Entry

20:53.020 --> 20:54.810
There is no way she'd be...

21:54.450 --> 21:55.540
You're...

22:14.390 --> 22:23.060
iro aseta page no kioku hitomi tojireba yomigaeru

22:14.390 --> 22:23.060
Memories on a faded page, they revive when I close my eyes

22:23.480 --> 22:32.240
adokenai shoujo no inori
habatakeyo kibou no sora he

22:23.480 --> 22:32.240
Prayers of an innocent girl
Fly away to the sky of hope

22:32.360 --> 22:36.660
nageku mamonaku  toki wa nagareru

22:32.360 --> 22:36.660
With no time to regret, time will flow

22:36.950 --> 22:41.750
hitori tachidomaru kedo

22:36.950 --> 22:41.750
Even though I stand alone

22:43.000 --> 22:48.510
yume mamoru shirabe  kuchizu samuno

22:43.000 --> 22:48.510
A tune to protect your dreams, I sing to myself

22:48.670 --> 22:53.010
hitobito ga nemuri ni tsukeba

22:48.670 --> 22:53.010
When people go into slumber

22:53.220 --> 23:00.930
mata au hi no negai tsumugeru deshou  ai no ito

22:53.220 --> 23:00.930
Their wish to unite can be woven. The thread of love

23:01.230 --> 23:11.360
yasashisa wo sasou  otogibanashi anata kara osowatta no yo

23:01.230 --> 23:11.360
Fairy tales that elicit kindness I learned that from you

23:11.530 --> 23:21.290
modorimashou  sotto ano koro no omoi ni

23:11.530 --> 23:21.290
Let us return gently to the memories of those times

23:30.970 --> 23:45.980
Next Time

23:30.970 --> 23:45.980
Looking Up at the Blue

23:32.550 --> 23:33.800
Let's play Shiritori!

23:33.890 --> 23:34.600
Monaka!

23:34.600 --> 23:35.510
Kaminarigumo.

23:35.510 --> 23:36.430
Mominoki.

23:36.430 --> 23:37.270
Kirigumo.

23:37.390 --> 23:38.140
Mozoku.

23:38.140 --> 23:38.930
Kumorigumo.

23:39.060 --> 23:39.770
Mokuzai.

23:39.770 --> 23:40.310
Iwashigumo.

23:40.310 --> 23:41.020
Momiji.

23:41.020 --> 23:41.770
Ji... Ji... Jiorogumo!

23:41.770 --> 23:42.850
Ji... Ji... Jiorogumo!

23:42.850 --> 23:43.600
Ji... Ji... Jiorogumo!

23:44.310 --> 23:45.320
Was that a pun?
